%N A398270 Array read by antidiagonals: T(n,k) is the feedback vertex set number of the grid graph P_n X P_k.
%C A398270 This is the least number of unit cells that must be removed from an n X n square board in order to avoid any cycles.
%C A398270 Note that the removal of cells is not required to leave a connected tree (only an acyclic graph).
%H A398270 Andrew Howroyd, <a href="/A398270/b398270.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..496</a> (first 31 antidiagonals)
%H A398270 Giedrius Alkauskas, <a href="https://klevas.mif.vu.lt/~alkauskas/math/square-sequence-alkauskas.pdf">Maximal subsets of n X n board without cycles</a>, 2022.
%H A398270 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/FeedbackVertexSetNumber.html">Feedback Vertex Set Number</a>.
%H A398270 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/GridGraph.html">Grid Graph</a>.
%F A398270 Conjecture: T(n,k) = n*k - A360920(n,k).
%F A398270 T(n,1) = 0.
%F A398270 T(n,2) = T(n-2,2) + 1 for n >= 3.
%F A398270 T(n,3) = T(n-4,3) + 3 for n >= 5.
%F A398270 T(n,4) = T(n-1,4) + 1 for n >= 2.
%F A398270 T(n,5) = T(n-8,5) + 11 for n >= 9.
%F A398270 T(n,6) = T(n-3,6) + 5 for n >= 6.
